.chapter 4
.h1 Conditional printing [conditional]
The markers If, Else and Endif select text, so one document prints as several
editions.  The old program had them as part of bulk printing and mail merge,
with a fourth marker, Merge.  Strata implements the three as conditional text.
Merge is a label only.
.h2 Origin [conditional-start]
The manual first held text for the people who build Strata: command lines of
the programs behind the Document Manager, environment variables and exit
codes.  On 14 November the project maintainer decided to purge that text, then
reversed the decision the same day:
.quote
  "Hold off on removing all that information from the documentation.  This is a
  perfect use of the conditional markers!"
.end
The work ran in two steps: the markers first, as a feature for every
document, then the text for developers between them.
.h2 Rules [conditional-rules]
.ix Variables
{Tab:rules} states the rules of the markers.  Examples of the comparison:
{c:10 > 9} is true because both sides are numbers; {c:10 < 9a} is true because
one side is text and the character 1 comes before 9; {c:undefined = undefined}
is true for two unset variables.
.tabcap rules Rules of the conditional markers
.table 14 50
Topic | Rule
Expression | A variable, an operator and a value, such as
 | {c:.STRATA_BUILD_TYPE # release}.  Operators: {c:=}, {c:#} (not equal),
 | {c:<}, {c:>}, {c:<=}, {c:>=}.  Conditions nest ten deep.
Variables | A string.  A name starts with a letter and holds letters, digits,
 | hyphens and underscores.  A value is printable 7-bit ASCII without a
 | quotation mark, at most 255 characters.  An empty value counts as not set;
 | an unset variable has the string {c:undefined}.
Special names | A name that begins with a period cannot be given by the user.
 | {c:.STRATA_BUILD_TYPE} tells whether the build is debug, release or asan.
Scope | The Document Manager passes the variables to the Editor, the Printer
 | and the Viewer and does not save them between runs.
Comparison | Numeric when both sides are digits that fit an unsigned 32-bit
 | integer; otherwise text, in the order of the ASCII codes, not of UTF-8.
Errors | A bad expression, an Else or Endif without an If, an If without an
 | Endif, nesting deeper than ten.  Each is reported with its position and
 | marked with a Print Error marker.  A bad expression is false.
.end
.h2 Printing and screen [conditional-how]
The Printer makes a filtered copy of the document before it writes LaTeX; the
text of branches that are not chosen is not copied.  Diagnostics keep the
positions of the original document.  The Editor shows all text and the
markers, because the project maintainer decided that nothing is hidden on the
screen.  The generator of the manual has a directive for each marker and stops
with a message in three cases:
1. A headline is left out in the middle of its parent in a document whose
headline numbers are typed.  A gap would remain.  Where the product makes the
numbers, as in this document, the Printer numbers what it prints.
2. Text that is always printed has a cross reference to a section that is not.
3. A condition is not closed in the file that opened it.
.h2 Use in this document [conditional-this]
Sections on defects of method, the measurement of passes, borders, faulty tests
and the organisation of the work stand inside an If marker with the condition
{c:.STRATA_BUILD_TYPE # release}.  Every build except a release prints them.
The contents, the lists and the section numbers follow the edition.  A
paragraph for developer builds only has no Else branch.  The one Else branch is
in {x:beginning-reading}, and its two texts differ.  Print the document from a
debug build and from a release build to compare.
.h2 Labels [conditional-honest]
Merge prints as {c:MERGE "name"} and its variable overrides nothing, because
Strata has no merge files.  The Figure, Picture, Table and Index markers are no
longer labels: the Printer makes the lists and the index from them and prints
nothing at their place.  The Batch Print Utility of the old program is not
implemented.
